<% content_for(:page_title) { "Developer Resources — #{Netd.portal_name}" } %>
<div class="netd-page netd-faq">
  <h1>Developer Resources</h1>
  <p>The portal's metadata can be reused through a REST API, an OAI-PMH interface and bulk downloads. The metadata comes from the
    participating institutional repositories; full texts stay in those repositories.</p>

  <h2 id="api">REST API</h2>
  <p>A read-only JSON API at <code><%= Netd.base_url %>/api/v1</code>. No key is needed. Each endpoint allows 120 requests a
    minute from one address (the export, 20 an hour). Field names in version 1 will not change.
    <strong><%= link_to 'Interactive reference', api_docs_path %></strong> ·
    <%= link_to 'OpenAPI 3 specification', '/api/v1/openapi.yaml' %></p>
  <table class="netd-about netd-api">
    <tr><th>Search records</th><td><code>GET /api/v1/records?q=malaria&amp;level=doctoral&amp;year=2015-2025</code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Filters</th><td><code>institution</code> (ids from <code>/institutions</code>, comma-separated), <code>level</code>
      (<code>masters</code>, <code>doctoral</code>, <code>postgraduate_diploma</code>), <code>year</code> (<code>2024</code> or <code>2015-2025</code>),
      <code>full_text</code> (<code>true</code>/<code>false</code>), <code>updated_since</code>, and exact <code>faculty</code>,
      <code>department</code>, <code>discipline</code>, <code>degree</code>, <code>subject_exact</code>, <code>supervisor_exact</code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Search one field</th><td><code>&amp;field=title</code> (also <code>author</code>, <code>supervisor</code>, <code>subject</code>)</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Sort and paging</th><td><code>&amp;sort=newest</code> (also <code>relevance</code>, <code>oldest</code>, <code>title</code>,
      <code>updated</code>); <code>&amp;page=2&amp;per_page=50</code> (20 by default, at most 100)</td></tr>
    <tr><th>One record</th><td><code>GET /api/v1/records/unza-123456789-9150</code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Institutions</th><td><code>GET /api/v1/institutions</code>: every <%= Netd.regulator_short_name %>-listed institution, with record counts and harvest status</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Statistics</th><td><code>GET /api/v1/stats</code>: counts by institution, degree level and year, and how complete each field is</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Everything</th><td><code>GET /api/v1/export.csv</code> or <code>/api/v1/export.jsonl</code>: all records in one file, refreshed every 6 hours</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p>Responses have <code>data</code>, and for lists <code>meta</code> (total, page, pages) and <code>links</code>
    (next, previous). Errors return <code>{"error": {"status", "title", "detail"}}</code> with status 400, 404 or 429.
    Browsers may call the API from other websites (CORS).</p>
  <pre class="netd-code">curl -s "<%= Netd.base_url %>/api/v1/records?q=malaria&amp;level=doctoral&amp;per_page=5"</pre>

  <h3>Search pages as JSON</h3>
  <p>Every search and record page is also available as JSON by adding <code>.json</code>, for example
    <code><%= Netd.base_url %>/catalog.json?q=malaria</code> or <code><%= Netd.base_url %>/theses/unza-9150.json</code>.
    This follows the website's search interface and its internal field names, which may change; use the REST API above for
    anything that must keep working.</p>

  <h2 id="fields-of-study">Fields of study (OpenAlex Topics)</h2>
  <p>Every record carries standard fields of study from <a href="https://openalex.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenAlex
    Topics</a> (CC0): 4 domains, 26 fields and 252 subfields, taxonomy as published by OpenAlex in November 2026. They are
    assigned by the portal's model <code>openalex-fos</code> (version 2) from each record's title and abstract: a sentence
    embedding (<code>sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2</code>) and a classifier trained on OpenAlex works labelled with their primary
    topic's subfield. When no subfield is likely enough, the broader field or domain is given, so every record has a value.
    Values are identified by their OpenAlex ids and URIs (for example <code>https://openalex.org/subfields/2739</code>).</p>
  <table class="netd-about netd-api">
    <tr><th>REST API</th><td><code>fields_of_study</code>: list of <code>{id, uri, name, level, field, domain, confidence}</code>;
      also listed under <code>derived</code> as <code>field_of_study</code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>OAI-PMH <code>etdms</code></th><td><code>&lt;subject scheme="OpenAlex"&gt;name&lt;/subject&gt;</code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>OAI-PMH <code>oai_dc</code></th><td>two <code>dc:subject</code> values per field: the name and its OpenAlex URI</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Repository subjects</th><td>kept unchanged as <code>subjects</code> (API) and plain <code>subject</code>/<code>dc:subject</code> (OAI-PMH)</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>OAI-PMH</h2>
  <table class="netd-about netd-api">
    <tr><th>Base URL</th><td><code><%= Netd.base_url %>/oai</code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Protocol</th><td>OAI-PMH 2.0; all six verbs (<code>Identify</code>, <code>ListMetadataFormats</code>, <code>ListSets</code>,
      <code>ListIdentifiers</code>, <code>ListRecords</code>, <code>GetRecord</code>)</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Metadata formats</th><td><code>oai_dc</code> (Dublin Core) and <code>etdms</code> (ETD-MS v1.1, for NDLTD)</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Sets</th><td>One per institution (for example <code>inst:unza</code>) and per degree level (<code>level:doctoral</code>, <code>level:masters</code>, <code>level:postgraduate-diploma</code>)</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Datestamps</th><td>When the record last changed in the portal (UTC, <code>YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ssZ</code>); use <code>from</code> and <code>until</code> for incremental harvesting</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Paging</th><td>100 records per response, with resumption tokens valid for 24 hours</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Identifiers</th><td><code>oai:<%= Netd.host %>:&lt;record id&gt;</code>, e.g. <code>oai:<%= Netd.host %>:unza-123456789-9150</code></td></tr>
  </table>
  <pre class="netd-code"><%= Netd.base_url %>/oai?verb=ListRecords&amp;metadataPrefix=etdms&amp;set=inst:unza</pre>

  <h2 id="csv">Contributing records by CSV</h2>
  <p>An institution without a repository that supports OAI-PMH can contribute its theses and dissertations as a CSV file,
    one row per thesis or dissertation. Start from the
    <%= link_to 'CSV template', '/netd-etd-template.csv' %>, which has one example row, and send the file to
    <a href="mailto:<%= Netd.contact_email %>"><%= Netd.contact_email %></a>. You can also publish it at a stable link, for example a Google
    Sheet published to the web as CSV, so that the portal reads the latest version every night. Records that are removed
    from the file are removed from the portal. Librarians: see the step-by-step <%= link_to 'guide for institutions', contribute_path %>.</p>
  <table class="netd-about netd-api">
    <tr><th>Required columns</th><td><code>identifier</code> (unique within your institution; letters, digits, <code>-</code> and <code>_</code>),
      <code>title</code>, <code>author</code>, <code>year</code> (four digits), <code>degree_level</code> (<code>Masters</code>, <code>Doctoral</code> or <code>Postgraduate Diploma</code>)</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Optional columns</th><td><code>degree</code>, <code>supervisor</code>, <code>faculty</code>, <code>department</code>,
      <code>discipline</code>, <code>subject</code>, <code>abstract</code>, <code>language</code> (e.g. <code>en</code>),
      <code>url</code> (the record's page at your institution), <code>pdf_url</code> (a public link to the full text), <code>rights</code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Several values</th><td>Separate them with <code>||</code> in <code>author</code>, <code>supervisor</code> and <code>subject</code>,
      e.g. <code>Phiri, Chanda||Mumba, Natasha</code>. Write names as Surname, Given names.</td></tr>
    <tr><th>File format</th><td>UTF-8 is preferred; files saved from Excel are also accepted. Commas or semicolons may separate columns.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Source code and contact</h2>
  <p>The portal is open source:
    <%= link_to 'github.com/lightonphiri/code-datalab26-netd_aggregator', 'https://github.com/lightonphiri/code-datalab26-netd_aggregator', target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener' %>.
    Questions: <a href="mailto:<%= Netd.contact_email %>"><%= Netd.contact_email %></a>.</p>
</div>
